<br>
For European Quake League Season 21 in 2016, Division 99 fielded four teams named after astronomical phenomena:<br>
<br>
d'Ninety Nine Black Hole<br>
d'Ninety Nine Mira<br>
d'Ninety Nine Nova<br>
d'Ninety Nine Pulsar<br>
<br>
7 players was assigned to Pulsar, but except for Mushi showing up and playing almost one map - Timon, Nidweyr, Meag and Baresi played all maps the remainder of the season.
<br><br>
Despite being put in random teams, handpicked by Ocoini, without knowing each other at all, very early they established a solid teamplay and communication. 
<br><br>
Good balance within the team, where Timon & Nidweyr usually took on the hard work clearing out enemy weapons and running quads, while Meag & Baresi kept positions and armors. 
Pulsar made some upsets to the better seeded teams during EQL21. 
<br><br>
Ocoinis astronomical teams were only supposed to last for that one season. And while the rest of the d99 teams went back to the mothership, the 4 Pulsars stayed together and kept playing.

